    "content": "The 2026 NCAA Men’s Basketball First Four, played March 17-18 at UD Arena in Dayton, Ohio, saw Texas and Howard open with victories, defeating NC State and UMBC respectively, while Prairie View A&M/Lehigh and Miami (Ohio)/SMU finalized the field of 64. These games determine the final spots in the NCAA Tournament bracket. Key 2026 Men's First Four Results & Schedule March 17: Howard 86, UMBC 83 March 17: Texas 68, NC State 66 March 18: No. 16 Prairie View A&M vs. No. 16 Lehigh (6:40 p.m. ET, truTV) March 18: No. 11 Miami (Ohio) vs. No. 11 SMU (9:15 p.m. ET, truTV) 2026 Women's First Four Schedule March 18: Nebraska vs. Richmond and Missouri State vs. Stephen F. Austin March 19: Southern vs. Samford and Virginia vs. Arizona State Important Details Location: All games are held at the University of Dayton Arena, Dayton, Ohio. What it is: The First Four consists of the four lowest-ranked conference champions (No. 16 seeds) and the four lowest-ranked \"at-large\" teams (often No. 11 seeds). Advancement: Winners move on to the first round of the NCAA Tournament, officially known as the Round of 64.",
